The src/Interfaces folder stores element locator files (per page or sub-function) using XPath, CSS selectors, etc. Review these to understand the locator file style and follow it when implementing new elements.

The src/DataTest folder stores data files used by scripts. Each file maps to a page—review and implement according to the framework's current style.

CRITICAL - POM DataTest File Management Rules:
+ Each page/module MUST have its own data file following the naming pattern: data_{page_name}.py
+ data_common.py is ONLY for common/shared data used across multiple pages
+ Before creating any new data file, ALWAYS check if a file for that page already exists in src/DataTest/
+ If the data file for a page already exists:
    - DO NOT create a new file with the same or similar name
    - ALWAYS add new data to the existing file
    - Read the existing file first to check if the data already exists
    - Only add the data if it doesn't exist yet in that file
+ If the data file does not exist for a new page:
    - Create a new file following the exact naming convention: data_{page_name}.py
    - Follow the existing code style and structure from other data files
    - Each data file MUST follow this structure:
        * Data dictionary with environment keys (local, sit, uat, pro)
        * Each environment contains language keys (en, ch, vi, etc.)
        * Each language contains the actual test data
+ Example: For "Betting Ticket Center" page:
    - Create data_betting_ticket_center.py (not data_btc.py, not data_betting.py)
    - Dictionary name: Data_BettingTicketCenter
+ DO NOT add page-specific data to data_common.py
+ This ensures clean POM architecture: one page = one data file = all test data for that page in one place

